S:Walter Jekyll (ed.), Jamaican Song and Story (London: David Nutt, 1907), Project Gutenberg #35410 (music as MusicXML), no. XCVIII, p. 199
N:Words and tune as Jekyll printed them (Allegretto). "I go to Galloway road (where there is a quarry). Girls and boys are breaking stones. They break them one by one, two by two... Choosing stones suggests choosing partners."
M:2/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=100
K:D
